{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>I have not sat with men of falsehood</b> — the opposite of the way of truth." "<b>hidden men</b> — from the root of ונעלם דבר (a thing is hidden), that they do things not so in secret. And some say: from the root עלם, that he is a lover of jest and mockery."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:36.826141045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}